    "turn_idx": 61,
    "turn_text": "as well as Democrats. Because nobody's got the answer to everything. And I've even And partly because of my seniorities, President Pro Tem, I've got a couple of beautiful offices in the cap, and I will loan them out to senators who want to have a family gathering or something. Both Republicans and Democrats, I just give them the key to say here, go and enjoy it. And I also had meetings in there of both Republicans and Democrats together. There's no press, no staff, just us. And we talk about family, we talk about our states, everything else. And then we usually find common ground on major legislation. I'll give you one example. I don't want to go too long on this, but about three years ago, we had the longest shutdown of the government in history. Donald Trump He said we hadn't put enough money in for his wall so he wouldn't sign the appropriations bills. Finally, four of us sat in that room. Dick Shelby, conservative Republican, and myself, needed a liberal Democrat, Kay Granger from Texas, a conservative Republican. And the four of us sat there. We talked about family. We talked about home. And then we talked about how do we get out of this mess? And after a couple of hours meeting there, we had it solved. We brought it to both the Republican and Democratic leaders. They said, look, if the four of you agree we'll accept it, then we reopen the government. But those things can be done. They can't be done if all you have is going to do sound bites or tweets or things like that. take out the most extreme, most extreme positions. There's too much of, my way is the only way we could take.",
